<title>FRANCE: Schneider down on Spie sale price report.</title>
<headline>Schneider down on Spie sale price report.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Schneider fell on Monday on a report in the Financial Times that Britain's AMEC Plc was expected to pay 25 million pounds for 40 percent of Schneider's Spie Batignolles unit, a price judged low by some investors, brokers said.</p>
<p>Schneider shares were down 2.04 percent at 254.40 francs at 1205 GMT.</p>
<p>One analyst said the price would be good if it were for Spie's public works business but low if it also covered the electrical material activities. Schneider confirmed on Friday that AMEC and Spie were in buyout talks.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
